    "sections": [
      {
        "body": "Completed protocol 2.0.0 asks about reversal follow-through, three-bar landing and incremental prediction in 6B, 6E, 6J and 6S Range XV 4/5 charts. These are OHLC-only exports, July 2017–October 2026. Chart/direction populations remain separate.",
        "id": "question",
        "kind": "text",
        "title": "Question and scope"
      },
      {
        "body": "The primary later F≥3 prediction result is negative: adding prior length or richer history gives no supported log-loss improvement beyond reversal geometry/context. Later length-two versus length-three contrasts remain inconclusive. A nominated colour-persistence association has a negative gross price mean; the other is inconclusive. A predicate with collapsed efficiency cutpoints adds no independent efficient-versus-choppy evidence.",
        "id": "findings",
        "kind": "text",
        "title": "Supported findings"
      },
